# Input system for the walker example (#545).
#
# inputUpdate turns devices into an INTENT rather than moving the character
# directly: the touch stick when active, else WASD/arrows (+ shift = walk). This
# is the same input the controller consumed inline before (updateWalkerMovement /
# updateThirdPersonController), just centralised — which is what makes multiplayer
# and input-switching cheap: a remote player's intent can arrive from net.rae
# instead of a device, and characterUpdate applies whichever intent it is given.
#
# InputState (the moveStick + UI input + intent bundle in the plan) is a later
# refinement; today the intent is a per-frame value threaded through updateApp,
# and the input/UI devices still live in app.rae's InputUi. Example-114 files are
# siblings that merge into one module. import block is app.rae's + sdl3.

#   physics.rae (fixed-step seam) · net.rae (multiplayer seam) · state.rae
#   (hot-reload + window persistence).
# app.rae keeps the App / state types, createApp, the loop, updateApp, frameBegin.
# Still to come: the input-intent split (#545) and turning the single character
# into a multiplayer-ready roster (#546/#547).
